# BP Dumper Dual-Client Sync

Dumper Apps has **two clients** that must stay feature-aligned for product
behavior. They intentionally differ only in how they obtain the Star Citizen
log folder.

| Client | Path | FS discovery |
|---|---|---|
| Standalone Python | `scripts/bp-dumper-py/` | Drive auto-scan / path prompt OK |
| Store (sandboxed) | `apps/bp-dumper-store/` | **FolderPicker + FutureAccessList only** — no disk scan |

Contract source of truth: `scripts/bp-dumper-shared/` (protocol + fixtures).

## When you change one client, update the other

If a change touches **shared product functionality**, apply the equivalent in
**both** clients in the same change set (or immediately after), and update
`scripts/bp-dumper-shared/PROTOCOL.md` / fixtures when the wire contract moves.

### Must stay in sync

- Webhook event `type` values and JSON fields
- Auth / version headers (`Authorization: Bearer dr_…`, `X-Dumper-Version`)
- Log parsing / mission correlation / blueprint resolution rules
- Live Mission Tracker publish fields and session ping semantics
- Version-gate behavior (`426` / update required)
- Full-history import **meaning** (what awards are imported, once-only UX)
- API key prompt / regenerate UX copy that members see

### Must NOT be copied into the Store client

- Drive scanning (`GetDriveType`, walking fixed disks for `StarCitizen`)
- Silent Program Files probing / auto-detect without user grant
- GitHub portable exe auto-update
- Any capability or API that requires `runFullTrust` or `broadFileSystemAccess`

Store access is limited to the folder the user picked (and persisted via
`FutureAccessList`). Do not “helpfully” reintroduce scan logic behind a toggle.

## Checklist before finishing a dumper feature

- [ ] Shared behavior documented / fixture updated in `bp-dumper-shared` if the wire or parse contract changed
- [ ] Python client updated **or** explicitly N/A (FS-discovery-only change)
- [ ] Store client updated **or** explicitly N/A (FS-discovery-only change)
- [ ] Commit scope stays `dumper` when cutting a Python release; Store packaging notes if Store binary/version must ship too
